I don&#39;t have a specific one to mention, but ...&nbsp;... based on what folks were writing in another thread, I played a game w/ Greatest Legacy, Team Leader Tachyon, Scholar, Argent Adept, and Santa Guise.&nbsp;HA HA HA HA HA HA HA! That was silly.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Tonight four of us played GI Legacy, Scholar, Prime Wardens AA, and Santa Guise.&nbsp; At one point I had out all six instruments and had used five powers on the same turn.   We were in the Enclave of the Endlings and Slamara came out, causing the villain and each hero to play the top card of their deck. 

&nbsp;

Scholar played Proverbs and Axioms. Santa Guise gave us all presents. GI Legacy gave Santa Guise an HP and a power user, so Santa Guise had AA flip his presents. That led to a whole series of cards, including multiple Instrumental Conjurations, Polyphoric Flares, Silver Shadows, and Arcane Cadence. I was able to use Arcane Cadence to put Silver Shadow on the bottom of the deck so that a later Polyphoric Flare present allowed AA to use his base power to play Silver Shadow off the bottom of the deck and use Silver Shadow to play another Polyphoric Flare out of AA&#39;s hand. After all that resolved, AA then took his turn with Proverbs and Axioms and set off the Lyre/Harp/Inspring Supertonic Chain.

&nbsp;

All on the environment turn.

&nbsp;

I thought those shenanigans were fun in the digital version, but they were even better with the visceral play of feeling and seeing all the cards and powers get played and used.
